––– comment –––
Filters on JSON keys must return the same rows with and without the JSON secondary index. Each table has 10000
padding docs so its chunk uses secondary indexes; each line compares No_SecondaryIndex with SecondaryIndex and
shows whether the secondary index was used.
- si_any_for: ANY(cond FOR x IN json.array) is replaced with a secondary index filter only when x is compared with
  constants ('=' with an int or a string, '<' '>' '<=' '>=' with an int, joined by AND/OR, the bounds in any
  order, an int64 bound too). Negations, functions,
  expressions over x, other attributes, float constants and INDEXOF() must not use it.
  Docs 1 i=[1,2] s=[x,y] f=[1.5,2.5], 2 [2] [y] [2.5], 3 [3] [z] [3.5], 4 [1] [x] [1.5], 5 [4,5] [w] [4.5].
- si_dup_vals: a value repeated in one array ([2,2], ["y","y"], ["Y","y"] for the case-insensitive string hash,
  two doubles that become one float) is stored once per document, so the document comes back once and COUNT(*)
  counts it once. Docs 1 [2,2] [y,y] [2.5,2.5], 2 [2] [y] [2.5], 3 [3] [Y,y] [3.5], 4 [4] [z] [1.00000001,1.00000002].
- si_types: a JSON secondary index column takes the widest type of the key in the chunk and is used only when it
  answers the filter type (int column: int =/IN/ranges, float column: float ranges, string column: string =/IN).
  A key that mixes numbers and strings is not indexed. Docs 1..4 below.
- si_excl: an excluding filter (!=, NOT IN, NOT BETWEEN) matches only documents that have the key, so it runs as a
  full scan; = keeps the secondary index. Docs 1 i=1 s=a, 2 i=2 s=b, 3 i=null s=null, 4 no keys.
––– block: ../base/start-searchd –––
––– input –––
manticore-load --quiet --json --port=9306 --init="SET GLOBAL auto_optimize=0; DROP TABLE IF EXISTS si_any_for; CREATE TABLE si_any_for (j JSON secondary_index='1');" --load="INSERT INTO si_any_for (id,j) VALUES (<increment>,'{\"i\":[99],\"s\":[\"pad\"],\"f\":[99.5]}')" --batch-size=1000 --threads=2 --total=10000 > /dev/null && manticore-load --quiet --json --port=9306 --init="DROP TABLE IF EXISTS si_dup_vals; CREATE TABLE si_dup_vals (j JSON secondary_index='1');" --load="INSERT INTO si_dup_vals (id,j) VALUES (<increment>,'{\"i\":[99],\"s\":[\"pad\"],\"f\":[99.5]}')" --batch-size=1000 --threads=2 --total=10000 > /dev/null && manticore-load --quiet --json --port=9306 --init="DROP TABLE IF EXISTS si_types; CREATE TABLE si_types (j JSON secondary_index='1');" --load="INSERT INTO si_types (id,j) VALUES (<increment>,'{\"int\":99,\"flt\":99.5,\"str\":\"pad\",\"intstr\":99}')" --batch-size=1000 --threads=2 --total=10000 > /dev/null && manticore-load --quiet --json --port=9306 --init="DROP TABLE IF EXISTS si_excl; CREATE TABLE si_excl (j JSON secondary_index='1');" --load="INSERT INTO si_excl (id,j) VALUES (<increment>,'{\"i\":99,\"s\":\"pad\"}')" --batch-size=1000 --threads=2 --total=10000 > /dev/null; echo $?
